From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add the GalaxyCore GC2053 sensor driver

Add a mainline V4L2 subdev driver for the GC2053, a 1920x1080 10-bit
Bayer sensor used on several Ingenic T31 cameras. The mode register
sequence, the 28-step analogue gain table, and the exposure/flip
register layout come from the Ingenic vendor sensor driver.

The driver uses the CCI register helpers, runtime PM, and the current
state-based subdev pad API. It exposes a single 1080p30 mode with
HBLANK/VBLANK, exposure, analogue gain, and mirror/flip controls.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2053.c
@@ -0,0 +1,930 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * GalaxyCore GC2053 CMOS Image Sensor Driver
+ *
+ * The register sequences and gain table are adapted from the Ingenic
+ * vendor sensor driver (sensor_gc2053_t31).
+ */
+
+#include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/i2c.h>
